Now I have a comprehensive picture. Let me implement the fixes. The bugs I'll fix:

**Bug 1: Operator precedence in categorize_message() (line 197-199)**
• `lower.contains("thread '") && (...) binds tighter than ||, so "assertion"` alone triggers TestAssertion
• Fix: add parentheses around the thread clause

Bug 2: Duplicate condition in `categorize_message()` (line 205-206)  
• `found \ appears twice; the second should be found ' to match Rust's alternative quoting in error messages
• Fix: replace duplicate with found '

**Bug 3: Over-broad categorize_python_message() (line 543-548)**
• lower.contains("failed") alone would match any message containing "failed" (e.g., "build failed", "connection failed"), misclassifying them as test assertions
• Fix: tighten to `test failed or tests failed`

